#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Admit, sync and revoke host access for people and projects.

Root's 0600 people/<user>.conf is UTF-8, one setting per line, no comments:
    member=hand
    member=<project> project-admin|developer
    locked=false
    laptop=<name> ssh-ed25519 <base64> <WireGuard base64> <IPv4>
Zero or more unique member lines appear in fixed order (hand first, then by
project name with project-admin before developer), followed by locked=true|false
and one laptop line per laptop in admission order. An older record with
role=project-admin, projects= and no member line is read as member=hand and
rewritten on its next write. Keys never go to output. Legacy laptop fields are
retained until card reconciliation replaces this input; no VPN peers are configured.

sync <project> runs for root or sudo -n from <project>'s unlocked recorded admin.
It copies the admin's plain private project.bundle and access.bundle into a fresh
0700 directory under /run/porelo-host/sync/, after removing what a sync that was
stopped or killed left there, verifies them through porelo project
verify --json under a DynamicUser unit without home or network, checks host:
against this host's forge/ca.pem DER
SHA-256, validates the whole developer diff before acting, reconciles accounts,
laptops, <project> developer memberships and the forge's developers team, and
records commit=, access_commit= and signer= lines in projects/<project>.conf.

With account= in forge.conf, admission creates the login and the porelo-<user>
gate; lock also revokes each <agent>-<user> a 6j host's agents= names.
Only new identities get tokens, atomically delivered as identity/token lines in
the person's 0600 /run/porelo-host/people/<user>/identities.tokens, for import and
removal. Its directory is the person's, 0700, in root's 0755 people directory;
links and another account's directory are refused. Lock and purge remove the
person's entire delivery directory without following links inside it.
Lock prohibits all those logins and deletes all their tokens through the TLS
admin API, trusting forge/ca.pem; its temporary admin token stays in memory.

Matrix uses host= from forge.conf and machine <host>-<user>, as porelo-matrix.
The first admin credential is atomically saved in root's 0600 matrix-admin.token;
credentials reach commands only on stdin. The machine token is written by the
person into private ~/.config/porelo/matrix directories, refusing links. Lock
uses expel alone to expel accounts and revoke registration, then removes the
person's local token. Expel answers "known": false, nothing expelled, for a
machine the homeserver never admitted, so lock has nothing to revoke there;
every refusal (78 or any other exit) stops the lock.

Validation precedes changes; publication of the record is last. Command failures
can leave partial system changes and are reported without their captured output.
Do not manually admit a partial account: inspect and remove its partial access
before retrying. Calls serialize on root's existing forge.conf, without creating
a lock file during validation. Purge removes the record; another purge then
refuses the unknown person with 65, leaving the same state.

The only test hook, _test_entry, exists only when imported under another name.
An installed call runs as __main__ with -I and accepts no path, identity, runner,
or hook overrides from arguments, stdin or the environment.
"""

